## WHY THIS BRIEF, AND WHO MAY DO IT
Tuesday never writes into this project's `.git` (hard rule 1: manage, don't do). The fold of a records branch is a Composer seat's, under its own brief, because the root checkout is dirty and holds untracked copies that collide (RELAYED, `Briefs/2026-10-22_B428_SEAT-R19_composer-records-fold-b426.md`, "WHY THIS BRIEF"; method precedent B428 and B344 Step 0b). **Composer's landing rule and verb** (the project's `CLAUDE.md` has no landing section; the practice is in the merge history and B428, MEASURED `git log --merges -4 main`: "Merge records/b426 ...", "Merge records/b339 ...", "Merge records/b328 ...", "Merge records/b321 ..."): quarantine only byte-equal colliding untracked root copies (`mv -n` to `.tools/<b>/_quarantine/<same relative path>`, never delete), then ONE `git merge --no-ff <branch>` per branch, a message naming the branch and what it folds, no push, no rebase, no squash.

